---
description: Синхронизировать master и пересоздать latest-only seed
agent: code
---

Run the helper directly from the current project directory. The command may be started from `master` or an active `itldev/*` worktree; the helper delegates source/master work to the main worktree.

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, run this lifecycle command with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` by default so the outer shell outlives the 3600-second Designer limit; if that limit is configured higher, raise the outer timeout too. Do not use `120000 ms` or other short defaults because the helper may launch 1C Designer/Enterprise operations.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action sync-master
```

The helper follows `SOURCE_REPOSITORY_UPDATE_MODE`: `workflow` updates the source infobase from its configured repository first, while `external` captures the current source state without mutating source. It exports and commits that configuration to installed-project `master` and always rebuilds the single latest branch seed including its event-log signature baseline. It does not refresh the current development branch. On failure, read only the last 80 lines of `logPath`; a failed seed must be recovered by repeating this command and must never be bypassed by copying source directly.

On success with a non-empty `userReport`, make the final response exactly that report rendered as Markdown. Otherwise report the exact seed sync ID and committed `master` SHA from the bounded result/log without adding unrelated actions.
